schemas/
└── institutional-graph.json
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "Legibility Office Institutional Knowledge Graph",
  "description": "Schema for representing institutions, governance relationships, capabilities, Digital Public Infrastructure, procurement, AI governance, and institutional memory within the Institutional Operating System (IOS).",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "graph": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "version": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "created": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date"
        },
        "nodes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/node"
          }
        },
        "edges": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/edge"
          }
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "version",
        "nodes",
        "edges"
      ]
    }
  },
  "$defs": {
    "node": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "Country",
            "Institution",
            "Ministry",
            "Agency",
            "Regulator",
            "DPI",
            "Capability",
            "Policy",
            "Framework",
            "Standard",
            "Dataset",
            "AI System",
            "Procurement System",
            "Knowledge Asset"
          ]
        },
        "name": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "description": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "country": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "attributes": {
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "name"
      ]
    },
    "edge": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "target": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "relationship": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "governs",
            "implements",
            "coordinates",
            "owns",
            "supports",
            "depends_on",
            "funds",
            "regulates",
            "procures",
            "integrates_with",
            "shares_data_with",
            "reports_to",
            "inherits_from",
            "strengthens",
            "monitors"
          ]
        },
        "weight": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "active",
            "planned",
            "retired"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "source",
        "target",
        "relationship"
      ]
    }
  }
}
Example (examples/generic/institutional-graph-example.json)
{
  "graph": {
    "version": "1.0",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "country-ng",
        "type": "Country",
        "name": "Nigeria"
      },
      {
        "id": "bpp",
        "type": "Agency",
        "name": "Bureau of Public Procurement"
      },
      {
        "id": "procurement-framework",
        "type": "Framework",
        "name": "Procurement Framework"
      },
      {
        "id": "digital-id",
        "type": "DPI",
        "name": "Digital Identity"
      },
      {
        "id": "institutional-memory",
        "type": "Capability",
        "name": "Institutional Memory"
      }
    ],
    "edges": [
      {
        "source": "country-ng",
        "target": "bpp",
        "relationship": "owns"
      },
      {
        "source": "bpp",
        "target": "procurement-framework",
        "relationship": "implements"
      },
      {
        "source": "procurement-framework",
        "target": "digital-id",
        "relationship": "depends_on"
      },
      {
        "source": "procurement-framework",
        "target": "institutional-memory",
        "relationship": "strengthens"
      }
    ]
  }
}
Purpose

This schema enables the repository to evolve into an Institutional Knowledge Graph, where:

Institutions become nodes.
Policies, standards, frameworks, AI systems, procurement systems, and DPI components are connected through explicit relationships.
The graph supports querying governance dependencies, institutional capabilities, interoperability, and policy impact.

Potential applications include:

Governance knowledge graphs
Institutional dependency mapping
AI-assisted policy reasoning
Procurement intelligence
Institutional memory systems
Digital twins of government
National capability modeling
